        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "<table><tr><td>Element Name</td><td>Type</td><td>Semantics</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>ListOfRootCertificateIDsType refer to 8.3.5.3.27</td><td>EVCC. These root certificates will be used by the EVCC to validate the SA certificates that are included in the CertificateInstallationRes. NOTE 3 The public key from the SA certificate that is included in the CertificateInstallationRes is used to verify the signatures on the CertificateInstallationRes.</td></tr><tr><td>MaximumContractCertificateChains</td><td>simpleType: xs:unsignedShort</td><td>Indicates the maximum number of contract certificate chains the EV wants to install at that time. This can be less than or equal to the maximum number of contract certificate chains the EV can store in its memory. NOTE 4 For example, if the EV can store 5 contract certificates and wants to install all 5, it will set MaximumContractCertificateChains parameter to 5. But if the same EV only wants to install 3 contract certificates, it will set MaximumContractCertificateChains parameter to 3 even though it can store a maximum of 5 contract certificate chains. It is important to note that if the SA only has 2 contract certificates available for this EV, it will only provide those 2 contract certificates even though MaximumContractCertificateChains is higher than the number of contract certificates that the SA has for this EV. However, if the SA has 7 contract certificates available and EV sent CertificateInstallationReq with MaximumContractCertificateChains set to 3, the SA will only provide 3 contract certificates based on the parameter PrioritizedEMAIDs.</td></tr><tr><td>PrioritizedEMAIDs</td><td>complexType: EMAIDListType Refer to 8.3.5.3.30</td><td>Optional: Indicates the list of EMAIDs referencing contract certificates that shall be installed into the EV. The EMAIDs are included in the order of priority from highest priority to lowest priority. The SA will use this parameter to filter the list of contract certificates to be installed in case MaximumContractCertificateChains is smaller than the number of contract certificates available at the SA and ensures that the EV gets the highest priority contract certificates it desires. If this parameter is omitted and the SA has more contract certificates for the EV than the maximum number of contract certificate chains the EV wants to install, indicated by MaximumContractCertificateChains in CertificateInstallationReq, SA may send any MaximumContractCertificateChains contract certificates (applicable to this EV) of the SA&#x27;s choice.</td></tr></table>",
